EXPERIMENT 3
Practicing DCL and TCL Commands

Ex.No.3: Practicing DCL and TCL Commands
Aim: To understand and practice DCL and TCL commands in SQL.
Objectives
Learn GRANT and REVOKE commands.
Understand COMMIT, ROLLBACK and SAVEPOINT.
Manage transactions effectively.
Control user access to database objects.
Algorithm
1. Create a database and table.
2. Insert sample records.
3. Practice GRANT and REVOKE.
4. Perform UPDATE operations.
5. Create SAVEPOINT.
6. Use ROLLBACK and COMMIT.
7. Verify the records.
SQL Program
CREATE TABLE Employee(
EmpID INT PRIMARY KEY,
Name VARCHAR(30),
Department VARCHAR(20),
Salary DECIMAL(10,2));
INSERT INTO Employee VALUES
(101,'Arun','HR',35000),
(102,'Priya','IT',45000),
(103,'Kavin','Finance',50000),
(104,'Divya','IT',55000);
GRANT SELECT ON Employee TO user1;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON Employee TO user1;
REVOKE INSERT ON Employee FROM user1;
REVOKE ALL ON Employee FROM user1;
SET AUTOCOMMIT=0;
UPDATE Employee SET Salary=48000 WHERE EmpID=102;
SAVEPOINT SP1;
UPDATE Employee SET Salary=60000 WHERE EmpID=104;
SELECT * FROM Employee;
ROLLBACK TO SP1;
COMMIT;
DELETE FROM Employee WHERE EmpID=101;
ROLLBACK;
SELECT * FROM Employee;
Exercise Questions with SQL Query Answers
1. Create a Book table.
CREATE TABLE Book(
 BookID INT PRIMARY KEY,
 Title VARCHAR(50),
 Author VARCHAR(40),
 Category VARCHAR(30),
 Price DECIMAL(8,2)
);
2. Insert five records.
INSERT INTO Book VALUES
(101,'Database System','Korth','Database',550),
(102,'C Programming','Dennis Ritchie','Programming',450),
(103,'Java Programming','Herbert Schildt','Programming',650),
(104,'Python Basics','Mark Lutz','Programming',700),
(105,'Computer Networks','Andrew Tanenbaum','Networking',600);
3. Grant SELECT permission.
GRANT SELECT ON Book TO student1;
4. Grant INSERT and UPDATE permissions.
GRANT INSERT, UPDATE ON Book TO student1;
5. Revoke UPDATE permission.
REVOKE UPDATE ON Book FROM student1;
6. Revoke ALL permissions.
REVOKE ALL ON Book FROM student1;
7. Disable Auto Commit.
SET AUTOCOMMIT=0;
8. Increase Programming book prices by 10%.
UPDATE Book SET Price=Price*1.10 WHERE Category='Programming';
9. Create SAVEPOINT.
SAVEPOINT SP_Book;
10. Update one book price.
UPDATE Book SET Price=800 WHERE BookID=104;
11. Rollback to SAVEPOINT.
ROLLBACK TO SP_Book;
12. Delete one record and rollback.
DELETE FROM Book WHERE BookID=105;
ROLLBACK;
13. Commit transaction.
COMMIT;
14. Display final table.
SELECT * FROM Book;
